            <div xml:id="d248">

                <pb facs="0288" n="276" xml:id="pg276"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">851D.001/36: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-04-12T13:00:00+02:00">April 12, 1943—1
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received April 12—8:33 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2565. Department’s 2264, April 10, noon. The Foreign Office has telephoned this
                    morning to say that Mr. Eden feels that a more appropriate procedure is to
                    request the Fighting French to recall Monsieur Bertaud to Africa and it is
                    taking action in this sense today. Pending reply from the Fighting French,
                    instructions are not therefore being sent the Governor of Trinidad as indicated
                    in our telegram No. 2548, April 11, noon.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Winant</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
